  "description_html": "<p>Whēkau or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/laughing_owl\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:laughing owl\">laughing owl</a> <i></i>\n</p><p>Photographed (in the Wellington Region?) between 1889 and 1910 by <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q42322068\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q42322068\"><span title=\"New Zealand photographer (1844-1936)\">Henry Charles Clarke Wright</span></a> (1844-1936).\n</p><p>\"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Worthy\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Trevor Worthy\">Trevor Worthy</a> (an expert on the subject) has stated that the photo is of a bird that was in the captivity of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Buller\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Walter Buller\">Walter Buller</a>. \nThe photo was taken in 1892 - of one of a pair of birds shipped to Rothschild.\"\n</p>\nThis bird belonged to Buller and was photographed during 1892 shortly before being shipped from New Zealand to a new owner, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Rothschild,_2nd_Baron_Rothschild\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Walter Rothschild, 2nd Baron Rothschild\">Walter Rothschild</a>, in England.",
